# Agent delegation (CPS paper project)

## Review → apply pipeline (preferred for professor feedback)

| Step | Agent | Model | Action |
|------|--------|-------|--------|
| 1 | **`cps-journal-reviewer`** | Opus (strong) | Journal + professor audit; Persian findings; **no edits** |
| 2 | **`cps-revision-applier`** | Composer Fast (weaker) | Apply finding IDs only; edit `main.tex` + sync `main.ltx` |

Checklist: `.cursor/rules/journal-review-checklist.mdc`  
Applier scope: `.cursor/rules/revision-applier-scope.mdc`

Example prompts:
- `cps-journal-reviewer: full audit + pdf4_comments crosswalk`
- `cps-revision-applier: apply R-001 R-005 R-010 from last review`

## Use `paper-reviewer-opus` subagent when the user asks to:
- Deep **numbers/RQ** audit vs raw JSON (narrower than journal-reviewer)
- Claim–evidence alignment, statistics-only pass

Use **`cps-journal-reviewer`** instead for section-by-section reviewer voice + professor PDF + clarity/structure/% notation.

## Use **`cps-related-work-reviewer`** when the user asks to:
- Strengthen **§2 Related work** only (2024–26 gaps, Conformal-ABR / SafeSABR / Kairos positioning)
- Draft positioning paragraph + table rows + bib stubs **without** full-paper audit

**Token rule:** this agent reads §2 + cited bib only — **not** full `main.tex`. Prefer it over `cps-journal-reviewer` for related-work tasks.

Example: `cps-related-work-reviewer: §2 only — gaps, table rows, draft paragraph, bib stubs. Persian report.`

Keep the parent conversation on Opus if no subagent is used; do not burn Opus tokens on full codebase search.

## Use `structure-strategist` then `structure-synthesizer` when the user asks to:
- Audit content **placement** across sections (MOVE/ADD/CUT/REORDER)
- Whether a formula, figure, table, or paragraph belongs elsewhere
- Structural redundancy, section order, appendix vs body
- See `.cursor/rules/structure-editing.mdc` — plan only; user approves before any edit

## Use `format-editor-fast` when the user asks to:
- Apply IEEE/Elsevier formatting rules (`font-ieee.mdc`) section by section
- Fix `Figure`→`Fig.`, math variable mode, operators, Latin, emphasis
- **Edit `main.tex` directly** — no Persian report (see `.cursor/rules/format-editing.mdc`)
- Optional `format-strategist` only if user wants audit without edit first

## Use `cps-mechanical-worker` subagent when the user asks to:
- Run `make_cps_paper_assets.py`, eval scripts, or shell checks
- Verify episode counts (204), co-design sync, git status, zip overleaf_upload
- Pull/sync/regenerate assets without interpretive analysis

## Use built-in subagents automatically:
- **Explore** — codebase/file search (fast model)
- **Bash** — terminal commands with verbose output

## Token discipline
- Paper numbers: read `new/src/paper/overleaf_upload/tables/macros_cps.tex` and `new/results/v18_certified/*/summary.json` only.
- Ignore paths in `.cursorignore` (models, raw_videos, encoded_multires, traces).
- Do not re-read entire `episodes.csv` unless paired Wilcoxon/bootstrap is needed.
